{
  "agent": "holmes-mcp",
  "artifact_text": "### Observations and locations\n1. Pod `notifications-worker-6784d8b8df-lk5l8` container logs report `ERROR notifications-worker: missing required setting SMTP_PASSWORD (environment variable is unset or empty)` followed by `FATAL notifications-worker: configuration invalid, exiting`.\n2. Deployment `notifications-worker` references Secret key `SMTP_PASSWORD` from Secret `notifications-smtp` with `optional: true` (`Deployment/notifications-worker` spec).\n3. Deployment change `CI-2398` records that Secret `notifications-smtp` uses key name `smtp-password` following platform conventions.\n\n### Ruled-out leads\n1. Resource constraints or OOM kills were ruled out because the container exited with `exitCode: 1` (`reason: Error`) immediately upon startup validation.\n2. Probe failures causing pod termination were ruled out because connection refused errors on readiness probes were secondary symptoms of the process crashing immediately.\n\n### Root cause\nDeployment `CI-2459` updated `notifications-worker` to reference Secret key `SMTP_PASSWORD` instead of the actual key name `smtp-password` stored in Secret `notifications-smtp`.\n\n### Recommended action\nThe notifications team should update the `notifications-worker` deployment manifest to reference `secretKeyRef.key: smtp-password` in `SMTP_PASSWORD` and redeploy.",
